      "text": "Yes, *Glassy-eyed*, titled *Meridian Glass* by Ama Owusu, is available in digital format. Here is a passage from the text:\n\n---\n\n**Chapter 1**\n\nThe workshop smelled of sand and heat and something else — something mineral, a smell that had no common name but that Nana had associated, since childhood, with the moment before things changed form. Her grandfather called it the smell of possibility, which she had always found romantic to the point of embarrassment. After twenty years, she simply called it home.\n\nShe arrived in the early morning, before anyone else, the way she always arrived on days she needed to think. The furnace had been banked overnight, and the glass pots still held the remnants of yesterday's work — a green that her grandfather had mixed in the 1970s from a formula written in a notebook she could no longer read...\n\n---\n\nThis excerpt provides an intriguing glimpse into the narrative and thematic elements of the novel. Since the text is accessible through library services, I recommend checking your local library or digital library platforms that might have the title available for borrowing or access. If you require more information or specific sections, please let me know!",
